{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"moldavite-evasive-elephant","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Two live-DC harness cells assert on an `OK:` line the canonical `sync` route no longer prints\n\n## Symptom\n\nThe scheduled **Live External Integration** run **31362329118** (2026-08-10, head\n`351e13bbda`) finished the DC harness at **3 failed, 59 passed, 1 xfailed** — the first\nnon-green DC harness since e369's exit-bar run 30964805133. Two of the three are a real\ntest-contract defect (the third is an unrelated runner flake, below).\n\nFailing cells, both in `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_reconcile_pass.py`:\n\n* `test_a_repeated_dc_reconcile_pass_writes_nothing`\n  — `AssertionError: second pass: the repeated pass did NOT report convergence`\n* `test_a_dc_created_ticket_carries_the_shared_jira_provenance`\n  — `AssertionError: inbound provenance pass: no OK line on stdout`,\n  `assert 'OK:' in 'invariants: scanned=1 filed=0 (cap=5)\\n'`\n\n## Root cause — the assertions are stale, the reconciler is correct\n\nCommit **`c87afedba8`** (\"Make bridge preview and sync primary\", 2026-08-08) switched these\ncells to `_run_bridge(repo, \"sync\", …)`. But\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py` prints the `OK: …` summary lines **only\nwhen `route not in {\"preview\", \"sync\"}`** — the canonical `sync`/`preview` routes suppress\nthat line deliberately. The pass in fact converged: stderr carries `BRIDGE_STATE: converged`\nand every differ counter is zero.\n\nSo the reconciler behaved correctly and the harness asserted on an output contract that the\nroute it was just pointed at does not emit. Run 30986591446 (2026-08-05), the last green one,\npredates `c87afedba8`, so run 31362329118 was the **first** live exercise of that change.\n\n## Fix\n\nRe-point the two helpers in `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_reconcile_pass.py`\n(`_assert_wrote_nothing` and `_assert_converged_writing_pass`, and their stale\n`__main__.py:456` citation) at the signal the `sync` route actually emits —\n`BRIDGE_STATE: converged` plus the zero differ totals — instead of the legacy `reconcile`\nroute's `OK:` line.\n\nDo NOT delete, skip, or `xfail` either cell to reach green: the standing operator constraint\non this harness forbids it, and the cells are testing something real.\n\n## Also observed in the same run (separate, do not conflate)\n\n`test_dc_mutations.py::test_outbound_create_stamps_both_provenance_markers` failed with\n`rebar create failed (exit 1): Error: git commit failed while holding lock: git timed out\nafter 30s` — runner I/O contention during a 40-minute live job, not an assertion. Track\nseparately if it recurs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] both cells assert on the output the canonical `sync` route emits (`BRIDGE_STATE:\n      converged` + zero differ totals), not on an `OK:` line, and the stale `__main__.py:456`\n      citation in the helpers is corrected\n- [ ] neither cell is deleted, skipped or `xfail`ed to reach green\n- [ ] a fresh **Live External Integration** run on `main` shows the DC harness with these two\n      cells PASSING and no new failures\n\n## Testing\n\n    gh workflow run \"Live External Integration\" --ref main","id":"9590-34f5-21a8-41fc","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Two live-DC harness cells assert on an OK: line the canonical sync route no longer prints"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786526159114535001,"uuid":"2b7a0566-eca5-4510-bdbe-3e1fab109993"}